{
  "tema": 8388,
  "slug": "posesivos-largos",
  "titulo": "Long-form possessive adjectives: mío, tuyo, suyo, nuestro",
  "subtitulo": "Un amigo mío, unas primas nuestras: the possessive after the noun.",
  "foto": "t01.jpg",
  "regla": "Long possessives go after the noun and agree with the thing owned: mío, tuyo, suyo, nuestro (-a, -os, -as). Un amigo mío = a friend of mine.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Besides the short possessives that go before the noun (**mi**, **tu**, **su**…), Spanish has a **long form** that goes **after** the noun. It does the same job, but it puts the emphasis on _whose_ it is, like English _a friend of mine_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Owner",
            "Masc. sing.",
            "Masc. pl.",
            "Fem. sing.",
            "Fem. pl."
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "mío",
              "míos",
              "mía",
              "mías"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "tuyo",
              "tuyos",
              "tuya",
              "tuyas"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted, ellos, ustedes",
              "suyo",
              "suyos",
              "suya",
              "suyas"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "nuestro",
              "nuestros",
              "nuestra",
              "nuestras"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Each one agrees in gender and number with the **thing owned**, not with the owner: **Marcos es amigo mío**, **Victoria es amiga mía**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Suyo** can mean _his, hers, its, yours (usted / ustedes), theirs_. When that's unclear, use **de** + the person: **un amigo de ella**, **la tabla de usted**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: the long form is the short one with a megaphone: **mi amigo** vs **un amigo mío**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Marcos es amigo ==mío==.",
              "en": "Marcos is a friend of mine."
            },
            {
              "es": "Victoria es amiga ==mía==.",
              "en": "Victoria is a friend of mine."
            },
            {
              "es": "Estos niños son hijos ==nuestros==.",
              "en": "These boys are our sons."
            },
            {
              "es": "Estas niñas son hijas ==nuestras==.",
              "en": "These girls are our daughters."
            },
            {
              "es": "Un primo ==tuyo== me arregló el carro.",
              "en": "A cousin of yours fixed my car."
            },
            {
              "es": "Esa tabla no es ==suya==, es de Beto.",
              "en": "That board isn't his, it's Beto's."
            },
            {
              "es": "¡Dios ==mío==!",
              "en": "My God!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
